<title>USA: Burlington says to sell unit to Sequa.</title>
<headline>Burlington says to sell unit to Sequa.</headline>
<dateline>GREENSBORO, N.C. 1997-05-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Burlington Industries Inc said Thursday it agreed to sell its textile chemicals subsidiary Sedgefield Specialties to Sequa Corp's Sequa Chemicals Inc for an undisclosed amount.</p>
<p>Burlington said the subsidiary will be operated by Sequa, and Burlington's textile manufacturing plants will continue to be leading customers for Sedgefield Specialties' products.</p>
<p>The sale is part of Burlington's strategy of concentrating on its core businesses, the company said.</p>
